nal work that helped create the neo soul genre."}], "places": [{"name": "Philadelphia, USA", "role": "Cultural Hub"}, {"name": "New York City, USA", "role": "Major Influence"}, {"name": "Los Angeles, USA", "role": "Music Industry Center"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: neo soul", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "neo-soul"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q268253", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_soul"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Neo soul played a crucial role in revitalizing interest in soulful music during the late 20th century, influencing artists and genres that followed, which led to a broader cultural appreciation for black musical heritage.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:08:58Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Music subgenre of soul music, back to the roots Created c. 1998.", "newValue": "Neo soul emerged as a distinct musical genre in the late 1990s, primarily in the United States, and is characterized by its fusion of contemporary R&B with elements of jazz, funk, and hip-hop. It is rooted in the cultural and musical traditions of African American communities, with influential artists like Erykah Badu, D'Angelo, and Jill Scott leading the charge. This genre not only revived classic soul sounds but also redefined artistic expression in popular music, making it a significant cultural movement that resonated globally.

The genesis of neo soul can be traced back to the mid-1990s, with the release of seminal albums such as D'Angelo's "Brown Sugar" in 1995 and Erykah Badu's "Baduizm" in 1997. These works revitalized interest in the soulful sounds of the past while incorporating modern production techniques and lyrical themes that addressed contemporary issues. The genre's rise was facilitated by platforms like BET's "Soul Train" and the emergence of independent record labels, which allowed artists to maintain creative control and reach wider audiences. By the early 2000s, neo soul had garnered critical acclaim and commercial success, establishing itself as a staple in the music industry.

